is called an _elliptic integral_.

The elliptic integral just defined can not, in general, be expressed in terms of elementary functions.

Exceptions to this are

(i) when _R_(_x_, _y_) contains no odd powers of \(y\).

(ii) when the polynomial \(y\)2 has a repeated factor.

We therefore exclude these cases.

